        "answer": {
          "short": "Expanding first is usually easier if dividing first would introduce fractions.",
          "worked": "In (a), dividing by 5 keeps the numbers whole. In (b), dividing by 6 introduces fractions, so expanding first keeps integer coefficients until the final step. In (c), subtracting 6 then dividing by 5 also keeps the numbers whole.",
